-- title:
--   Theorem 8.1 — the complete 3-tensor transporter in a generated subgroup in time $q^{O(n_1+n_2+n_3)}\mathrm{poly}(\mathrm{InSize})$
-- statement:
--   There are a deterministic algorithm and a constant $C$ with the following property. Let $\mathbb F_q$ be a finite field (given by a presentation), $U_i=\mathbb F_q^{n_i}$, $T,T'\in U_1\otimes U_2\otimes U_3$, and let $\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}\le\mathrm{GL}(U_1)\times\mathrm{GL}(U_2)\times\mathrm{GL}(U_3)$ be generated by a given list. On an input of length $L$ the algorithm halts within
--   $$
--   C\cdot q^{\,C(n_1+n_2+n_3)}\cdot(L+2)^C
--   $$
--   steps and outputs the transporter $\mathrm{Trans}_{\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}}(T,T')=\{(g_1,g_2,g_3)\in\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}:(g_1\otimes g_2\otimes g_3)T=T'\}$ as a coset: emptiness if it is empty, and otherwise one element $u$ of it together with generators of exactly $\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}}(T)=\mathrm{Trans}_{\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}}(T,T)$, so that $\mathrm{Trans}_{\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}}(T,T')=u\,\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}}(T)$.
--
--   This strengthening of Theorem 1.2 (arbitrary subgroups $\Gamma_{\mathrm{in}}$, full coset output) is the form used inside the cohomology transports of the group isomorphism algorithm.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The instance code is `encTransInst`; elements are output as the coordinates of their three matrices.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - reading: q^O(n1+n2+n3) poly(InSize) → C · q^(C(n₁+n₂+n₃)) · (L+2)^C steps of one machine, L the code length, C chosen before every parameter; reason: one absolute constant per O(·) and per poly(·)
--   - encoding: arrays / tensors over F_q → a presented field `P : FieldPres` (q = p^e) in the input, entries in power-basis coordinates; reason: an algorithm over every F_q needs the field in its input; every finite field has a presentation
--   - reading: output elements with straight-line programs in the input generators (§3.5, p.19) → output elements written as themselves (label tables, matrix entries, permutation images); reason: for permutation and matrix groups each form is computable from the other in polynomial time (constructive membership, §3.5 (i), p.20); the coset is the same
--   - encoding: generators of Γin ≤ ∏ GL(U_i) → an arbitrary finite list of triples of invertible matrices, Γin its generated subgroup; reason: the paper's input; the empty list gives Γin = 1
-- source:
--   Qiao, Zhang, Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Theorem 8.1, p.71 (PDF p.75)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HMBinPacking_OutputsWithin
import Definitions.Def_GroupIsoPoly_CosetCorrect
import Definitions.Def_GroupIsoPoly_encAnswer
import Definitions.Def_GroupIsoPoly_encTransInst

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace GroupIsoPoly

open AvgCaseTI (FieldPres)

/-- **Theorem 8.1 (Complete 3-tensor isomorphism).**

Qiao, Zhang, *Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order*, preprint,
Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Theorem 8.1, p.71 (PDF p.75): "Given T, T′ ∈
U1 ⊗Fq U2 ⊗Fq U3 and generators of Γin ≤ ∏_{i=1}^3 GL(Ui), there is a deterministic algorithm
computing TransΓin(T, T′) := {(g1, g2, g3) ∈ Γin : (g1 ⊗ g2 ⊗ g3)T = T′} in time
q^O(n1+n2+n3) poly(InSize), where InSize is the total input bit length. The output is emptiness, or a
representative u and generators of StabΓin(T) := TransΓin(T, T), representing the set u StabΓin(T)."

There are one deterministic machine `M` and one constant `C` such that for every presented field
`F_q`, all `n₁, n₂, n₃`, all `T, T′ ∈ F_q^{n₁} ⊗ F_q^{n₂} ⊗ F_q^{n₃}` and every list of generators of a
subgroup `Γin ≤ GL(n₁, q) × GL(n₂, q) × GL(n₃, q)`, `M` on the code of the instance (length `L`) halts
within `C · q^(C(n₁+n₂+n₃)) · (L + 2)^C` steps and outputs a correct coset answer: emptiness if
`Trans_Γin(T, T′) = ∅`, otherwise some `u ∈ Trans_Γin(T, T′)` and a list generating exactly
`Stab_Γin(T)`.

**Formalization Note.** Elements are output as the coordinates of their three matrices. -/
theorem theorem_8_1 :
    ∃ M : Turing.TM2ComputableAux Bool Bool, ∃ C : ℕ,
      ∀ (P : FieldPres) (n₁ n₂ n₃ : ℕ) (T T' : Array3 P.F n₁ n₂ n₃)
        (gens : List (GL3 P.F n₁ n₂ n₃)),
        ∃ ans : Option (GL3 P.F n₁ n₂ n₃ × List (GL3 P.F n₁ n₂ n₃)),
          CosetCorrect (transIn gens T T') (transIn gens T T) ans ∧
            HMBinPacking.OutputsWithin M (encTransInst P n₁ n₂ n₃ T T' gens)
              (encAnswer (ans.map fun x => (gl3Nats P x.1, x.2.map (gl3Nats P))))
              (C * P.q ^ (C * (n₁ + n₂ + n₃)) *
                ((encTransInst P n₁ n₂ n₃ T T' gens).length + 2) ^ C) := by sorry

end GroupIsoPoly
